<article class="env-lemma" id="0EXK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EXK">Lemma <span data-tag="0EXK">9.15.4</span>.</a> Let $E/F$ be a normal algebraic field extension. Then the subextension $E/E_{sep}/F$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/030K" data-tag="030K">9.14.6</a> is normal. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If the characteristic is zero, then $E_{sep} = E$, and the result is clear. If the characteristic is $p > 0$, then $E_{sep}$ is the set of elements of $E$ which are separable over $F$. Then if $\alpha \in E_{sep}$ has minimal polynomial $P$ write $P = c(x - \alpha )(x - \alpha _2) \ldots (x - \alpha _ d)$ with $\alpha _2, \ldots , \alpha _ d \in E$. Since $P$ is a separable polynomial and since $\alpha _ i$ is a root of $P$, we conclude $\alpha _ i \in E_{sep}$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>